(899585, 101206, 19959, '<td valign="top">LOL,<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments guys. I had some fun on this one. My wife thought I was crazy, crouching in front of my oven with a black sock up one arm ''animating'' a cookie for the camera!!!<br/> <br/>Chris</td>', 'LOL, Thanks for the comments guys. I had some fun on this one. My wife thought I was crazy, crouching in front of my oven with a black sock up one arm ''animating'' a cookie for the camera!!! Chris', '2004-09-08 09:45:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(899874, 101308, 18191, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Great subject matter here. I like the interesting tone of the orange and the yellows scattered on the stonework. You showed this very nicely.<br/> <br/>A couple of criticisms...I understand the way you tilted the camera to achieve an effect of exagerrated heigh but this does not work here for two reasons. One, there are no verticals that are parallel to the frame. Also, the top of the building is just cut-off to that there is no breathing room. Try to include not just the whole building but also some part of the sky above it to balance out the photo. My last bit of criticism is that it seems to focus is off.<br/> <br/>Good photo, nice attempt. Next time you get over there try again. Good luck!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments, or concerns, feel free to PM me.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Great subject matter here. I like the interesting tone of the orange and the yellows scattered on the stonework. You showed this very nicely. A couple of criticisms...I understand the way you tilted the camera to achieve an effect of exagerrated heigh but this does not work here for two reasons. One, there are no verticals that are parallel to the frame. Also, the top of the building is just cut-off to that there is no breathing room. Try to include not just the whole building but also some part of the sky above it to balance out the photo. My last bit of criticism is that it seems to focus is off. Good photo, nice attempt. Next time you get over there try again. Good luck! If you have any questions, comments, or concerns, feel free to PM me.', '2004-09-08 12:52:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(899996, 101410, 17613, '<td valign="top">You deserve the ribbon just for the work you put in. Great photo, well done.</td>', 'You deserve the ribbon just for the work you put in. Great photo, well done.', '2004-09-08 14:35:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(900197, 101314, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi From the Critique Club<br/>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</b> <br/> <br/>This is one of those shots that will probably be ignored or loved. As an image it''s a sweet enough shot of the cat but as a challenge entry I wonder what you would have expected. Personally I think the literal link to the Fairy tale would not go down well with voters but perhaps it may be just too unimaginative in its execution. If the cat was in aboot it may have rated better!<br/> <br/>It''s well composed and the items arranged nicely, although the flat lighting and bland colour has not helped much.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', 'Hi From the Critique Club. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  This is one of those shots that will probably be ignored or loved. As an image it''s a sweet enough shot of the cat but as a challenge entry I wonder what you would have expected. Personally I think the literal link to the Fairy tale would not go down well with voters but perhaps it may be just too unimaginative in its execution. If the cat was in aboot it may have rated better! It''s well composed and the items arranged nicely, although the flat lighting and bland colour has not helped much. CheersJon', '2004-09-08 16:02:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(900212, 101359, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi From the Critique Club<br/>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</b> <br/> <br/>Very cute subject here. To get the negatives out of the way though - it relies heavily on the title to succeed in the challenge and outside of it I doubt anyone would guess the challenge without knowing. The pool of light is also very hot causing blown highlights. This is indeed a toad by the way and shouldn''t one kiss a frog for a prince?  Not me though - I''m heterosexual.  ; )<br/> <br/>Good composition but I bet you could have got closer which would have improved the shot greatly, getting the viewer more involved.</td>', 'Hi From the Critique Club. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  Very cute subject here. To get the negatives out of the way though - it relies heavily on the title to succeed in the challenge and outside of it I doubt anyone would guess the challenge without knowing. The pool of light is also very hot causing blown highlights. This is indeed a toad by the way and shouldn''t one kiss a frog for a prince?  Not me though - I''m heterosexual.  ; ) Good composition but I bet you could have got closer which would have improved the shot greatly, getting the viewer more involved.', '2004-09-08 16:09:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(900233, 101389, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi From the Critique Club<br/>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</b> <br/> <br/>This is a great concept for the challenge. Very nice indeed.<br/> <br/>Its weaknesses though are what have separated it from ordinary and greatness. In particular the lighting (flash) has killed the sense of 3rd party observation. It''s plain dull to see light face-on like this I''m afraid. You would have greatly enhanced this image by using directional light - perhaps from above &amp; behind, maybe softening it so that it looked liek the light from a kitchen in the giant''s home.<br/> <br/>You may also have tried a narrow DOF to focus on the golden egg. Well composed subject too.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', 'Hi From the Critique Club. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  This is a great concept for the challenge. Very nice indeed. Its weaknesses though are what have separated it from ordinary and greatness. In particular the lighting (flash) has killed the sense of 3rd party observation. It''s plain dull to see light face-on like this I''m afraid. You would have greatly enhanced this image by using directional light - perhaps from above & behind, maybe softening it so that it looked liek the light from a kitchen in the giant''s home. You may also have tried a narrow DOF to focus on the golden egg. Well composed subject too. CheersJon', '2004-09-08 16:17:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(900281, 100859, 17148, '<td valign="top">I know this is a grasshoper, that''s why I put the title on it</td>', 'I know this is a grasshoper, that''s why I put the title on it', '2004-09-08 16:44:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(900320, 101206, 19425, '<td valign="top">congrats on your 13th place finish...when voting for this pic, i was curious on how you did it....im so happy you are one of those people that actually explain how you did it...awesome!....<br/> <br/>black sock...hehehe...thats a great idea....funny about your wife...mine makes fun of me for some of the same reasons with my pictures....</td>', 'congrats on your 13th place finish...when voting for this pic, i was curious on how you did it....im so happy you are one of those people that actually explain how you did it...awesome!.... black sock...hehehe...thats a great idea....funny about your wife...mine makes fun of me for some of the same reasons with my pictures....', '2004-09-08 17:04:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(900859, 101325, 6870, '<td valign="top">This is really delightful. Wonderful challenge articulation. Just a wonder to look at!</td>', 'This is really delightful. Wonderful challenge articulation. Just a wonder to look at!', '2004-09-08 21:47:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(900862, 100207, 6870, '<td valign="top">That expression says it all. Kudos to you and your lovely wife!</td>', 'That expression says it all. Kudos to you and your lovely wife!', '2004-09-08 21:47:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(900864, 101410, 6870, '<td valign="top">Nice clarity and reminds us so effectively of the story. Super job!</td>', 'Nice clarity and reminds us so effectively of the story. Super job!', '2004-09-08 21:48:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(901272, 101002, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/>This photograph is well taken. It is properly exposed and sharp and the composition is great. However, it would have to fit in the outer limits of the challenge, if it is to fit at all. With the challenge of fairy tales you had the opportunity to stretch the truth and called it Pinochio. This would have fooled some people.<br/>  I appreciate your sense of humor and can imagine the glitter in your eyes, but the voting block was definetly wanted the romanric and fanciful. Again, your photographic abilities are commended and so is your sense of humor because I believe you knew the end result. Your port is very noce and interesting. I like that coffee can bread. Funny.</td>', 'from the critique club:This photograph is well taken. It is properly exposed and sharp and the composition is great. However, it would have to fit in the outer limits of the challenge, if it is to fit at all. With the challenge of fairy tales you had the opportunity to stretch the truth and called it Pinochio. This would have fooled some people.  I appreciate your sense of humor and can imagine the glitter in your eyes, but the voting block was definetly wanted the romanric and fanciful. Again, your photographic abilities are commended and so is your sense of humor because I believe you knew the end result. Your port is very noce and interesting. I like that coffee can bread. Funny.', '2004-09-09 01:32:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(901289, 101353, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/> <br/>This is an interesting image with a strong foreground against a majestic background. Its problem in the challenge may be due to the lack of color, the harsh light, namely the time of exposure. Since this challenge was advanced editing I would have made a solid or gradient layer and used a either a red or a blue and then select a low opacity, just enough to bring some magic into the image. So there is nothing that is particularly wrong with the shot except that the enchantment aspect was not exploited.<br/> <br/>You certainly had a good idea and you managed to make a very good capture. The composition is good. My only advise is that when you shoot still subjects, I would opt for the lowest ISO and take advantage of the smallest aperture even if you have to go down to 60th of a second which you can very well manage by holding the camera steady.<br/> <br/>Another idea for this subject is to have gone for a close up at ground level of the plants. Drop a red or blue tint layer, as explained above and bingo, the enchantment is there.</td>', 'from the critique club: This is an interesting image with a strong foreground against a majestic background. Its problem in the challenge may be due to the lack of color, the harsh light, namely the time of exposure. Since this challenge was advanced editing I would have made a solid or gradient layer and used a either a red or a blue and then select a low opacity, just enough to bring some magic into the image. So there is nothing that is particularly wrong with the shot except that the enchantment aspect was not exploited. You certainly had a good idea and you managed to make a very good capture. The composition is good. My only advise is that when you shoot still subjects, I would opt for the lowest ISO and take advantage of the smallest aperture even if you have to go down to 60th of a second which you can very well manage by holding the camera steady. Another idea for this subject is to have gone for a close up at ground level of the plants. Drop a red or blue tint layer, as explained above and bingo, the enchantment is there.', '2004-09-09 01:51:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(901731, 100207, 22866, '<td valign="top">Awesome.  I can see a lot of work went into this shot.  Great job.  Should of scored higher than 7.4.</td>', 'Awesome.  I can see a lot of work went into this shot.  Great job.  Should of scored higher than 7.4.', '2004-09-09 11:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(901836, 100591, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Camazine...<br/> <br/>This is a neat humor photo, but I couldn''t find much significance with it outside of that.  I''m sure this photo also suffered from a lack of a tie to a ''known'' fairy tale also.  Getting close here was a good idea, but the light from the camera flash doesn''t really create visual impact.  I can''t really offer much critique beyond that....<br/> <br/>Better luck next time :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Camazine... This is a neat humor photo, but I couldn''t find much significance with it outside of that.  I''m sure this photo also suffered from a lack of a tie to a ''known'' fairy tale also.  Getting close here was a good idea, but the light from the camera flash doesn''t really create visual impact.  I can''t really offer much critique beyond that.... Better luck next time :) John Setzler', '2004-09-09 13:21:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(902438, 101353, 12962, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> from the critique club:<br/> <br/>This is an interesting image with a strong foreground against a majestic background. Its problem in the challenge may be due to the lack of color, the harsh light, namely the time of exposure. Since this challenge was advanced editing I would have made a solid or gradient layer and used a either a red or a blue and then select a low opacity, just enough to bring some magic into the image. So there is nothing that is particularly wrong with the shot except that the enchantment aspect was not exploited.<br/> <br/>You certainly had a good idea and you managed to make a very good capture. The composition is good. My only advise is that when you shoot still subjects, I would opt for the lowest ISO and take advantage of the smallest aperture even if you have to go down to 60th of a second which you can very well manage by holding the camera steady.<br/> <br/>Another idea for this subject is to have gone for a close up at ground level of the plants. Drop a red or blue tint layer, as explained above and bingo, the enchantment is there. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>THANK YOU very much, Daniel.  The post processing procedures that you''ve suggested are just what I was looking for but didn''t know how to do.  This is such a good learning experience.  I actually have pictures from the ground level but like this photo, they were also a bit flat ... I had no choice for the lighting because I went to the park at noon - I only had a day to visit.  I will surely apply your suggestions to my other pictures.  Thanks again!</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: from the critique club: This is an interesting image with a strong foreground against a majestic background. Its problem in the challenge may be due to the lack of color, the harsh light, namely the time of exposure. Since this challenge was advanced editing I would have made a solid or gradient layer and used a either a red or a blue and then select a low opacity, just enough to bring some magic into the image. So there is nothing that is particularly wrong with the shot except that the enchantment aspect was not exploited. You certainly had a good idea and you managed to make a very good capture. The composition is good. My only advise is that when you shoot still subjects, I would opt for the lowest ISO and take advantage of the smallest aperture even if you have to go down to 60th of a second which you can very well manage by holding the camera steady. Another idea for this subject is to have gone for a close up at ground level of the plants. Drop a red or blue tint layer, as explained above and bingo, the enchantment is there.   THANK YOU very much, Daniel.  The post processing procedures that you''ve suggested are just what I was looking for but didn''t know how to do.  This is such a good learning experience.  I actually have pictures from the ground level but like this photo, they were also a bit flat ... I had no choice for the lighting because I went to the park at noon - I only had a day to visit.  I will surely apply your suggestions to my other pictures.  Thanks again!', '2004-09-09 20:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(902628, 101206, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>This photo tells a definite story. The motion blur is perfect and "makes" the picture. Good lighting, and effective composition. A couple of minor distractions: the blurred/smeared sugar on his right side and the line (oven door?) in the background. But overall very creative and well done.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  This photo tells a definite story. The motion blur is perfect and "makes" the picture. Good lighting, and effective composition. A couple of minor distractions: the blurred/smeared sugar on his right side and the line (oven door?) in the background. But overall very creative and well done.', '2004-09-09 22:54:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(902707, 100694, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>A beautiful portrait that shows off your signature ability to capture the souls of children. The model has a great pose and expression, and I like the hair covering half her face. The side of her nose is perhaps a bit bright; I find the contrast with the shadows a bit distracting. The photo is otherwise well-exposed. Her shoulder is even brighter, but that works well, giving the photo an overall light fairy tale look. Great photo!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  A beautiful portrait that shows off your signature ability to capture the souls of children. The model has a great pose and expression, and I like the hair covering half her face. The side of her nose is perhaps a bit bright; I find the contrast with the shadows a bit distracting. The photo is otherwise well-exposed. Her shoulder is even brighter, but that works well, giving the photo an overall light fairy tale look. Great photo!', '2004-09-09 23:58:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(902767, 100207, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>A great photo, well deserving of a ribbon! The overall light tone fits the subject well, giving the desired fairy tale feeling. Focus is perfect and the shallow DOF adds depth and, combined with the large leaf, gives the impression of a macro shot of a small fairy. Very effective! Colors are perfect, as is the wonderfully impish expression.<br/> <br/>Since you requested a critique, I''ll point out the only problem I see, and it is very minor, not detracting from the overall image. The glare on the lips and, to a lesser extent, the nose is a bit bright. Discreet application of the Burn tool could tone it down to better match the rest of the image.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  A great photo, well deserving of a ribbon! The overall light tone fits the subject well, giving the desired fairy tale feeling. Focus is perfect and the shallow DOF adds depth and, combined with the large leaf, gives the impression of a macro shot of a small fairy. Very effective! Colors are perfect, as is the wonderfully impish expression. Since you requested a critique, I''ll point out the only problem I see, and it is very minor, not detracting from the overall image. The glare on the lips and, to a lesser extent, the nose is a bit bright. Discreet application of the Burn tool could tone it down to better match the rest of the image.', '2004-09-10 00:31:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(903107, 101410, 11738, '<td valign="top">Thanks for sharing the info on this shot.  Great work and imagination.  I took a look at your two outtakes and I still prefer the one you finally submitted.  Keep it up dude.</td>', 'Thanks for sharing the info on this shot.  Great work and imagination.  I took a look at your two outtakes and I still prefer the one you finally submitted.  Keep it up dude.', '2004-09-10 09:35:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(904656, 101325, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>It looks like you snuck into Fairy Tale Land and took a candid shot of one of its inhabitants. The vignetting puts the focus of attention on the subject where it belongs while allowing the setting to provide useful context without unwanted distraction. It''s a lot more effective than cropping would have been. The softness and saturated colors create the desired ethereal effect, although I personally think both are just a bit overdone. Overall, a wonderful photo, but you already knew that!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  It looks like you snuck into Fairy Tale Land and took a candid shot of one of its inhabitants. The vignetting puts the focus of attention on the subject where it belongs while allowing the setting to provide useful context without unwanted distraction. It''s a lot more effective than cropping would have been. The softness and saturated colors create the desired ethereal effect, although I personally think both are just a bit overdone. Overall, a wonderful photo, but you already knew that!', '2004-09-11 11:38:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(904665, 100989, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>A great portrait! The model is beautiful and hope shines from her face. The lighting is perfect, with just enough soft shadow to define the graceful form of her face and providing nice glints in her eyes. Focus is nicely soft but the DOF is too narrow; an aperture one step smaller (f/4) would have put the whole subject in focus while still keeping the background unobtrusively blurry. But that''s minor; it''s a great photo as it is.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  A great portrait! The model is beautiful and hope shines from her face. The lighting is perfect, with just enough soft shadow to define the graceful form of her face and providing nice glints in her eyes. Focus is nicely soft but the DOF is too narrow; an aperture one step smaller (f/4) would have put the whole subject in focus while still keeping the background unobtrusively blurry. But that''s minor; it''s a great photo as it is.', '2004-09-11 12:03:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(904697, 101116, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>The subject is certainly appropriate for the challenge, but this interpretation isn''t very compelling. A vertical format would have worked better, not only having the entire figure included but allowing a more dynamic composition. An organic element such as a real plant would add interest as well. But the photo would benefit the most from more interesting lighting. Having the key light more to the side would better bring out the three dimensional form.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  The subject is certainly appropriate for the challenge, but this interpretation isn''t very compelling. A vertical format would have worked better, not only having the entire figure included but allowing a more dynamic composition. An organic element such as a real plant would add interest as well. But the photo would benefit the most from more interesting lighting. Having the key light more to the side would better bring out the three dimensional form.', '2004-09-11 12:34:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(905229, 100699, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/>Well, this was a stroke of genius. A novel concept, creative use of common objects and a youthful hand. I can not over emphasize how clever this comp is. I happen to like the cow out of the focus range, but you could have shot this at f4 with 1/15. However, I like it the way it is because the eye is drawn to the main subject.<br/> Presented with such a complete image I have nothing to add except that I look forward to another effort. You have a good imagination and you are able to express it in a most convincing manner.</td>', 'from the critique club:Well, this was a stroke of genius. A novel concept, creative use of common objects and a youthful hand. I can not over emphasize how clever this comp is. I happen to like the cow out of the focus range, but you could have shot this at f4 with 1/15. However, I like it the way it is because the eye is drawn to the main subject. Presented with such a complete image I have nothing to add except that I look forward to another effort. You have a good imagination and you are able to express it in a most convincing manner.', '2004-09-11 22:05:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(905234, 100824, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique Club:<br/> <br/>This was a very smart concept and even the choice for b/w was also wise. The only weakness is in the execution of the halo. Since the comp is okay and the photography is okay, let me concentrate on the effect.<br/>The way to do this is to select the figure after you have done all the levels adjustments, etc. After selection, copy the layer. Copy your background and draw an oval with 40 or 60 pixel feather. One way to finish is to fill the oval with white and then reduce the opacity to your liking. Then you paste the layer of the girl you originally copied.<br/> <br/>In essence, you have the actual background. On top you have a copy of the background and this layer is applied with just enough opacity to accentuate the halo. On top of this you paste the girl and the halo appears to come from the back while preserving the detail of the girl. This is superior to selecting her inversing and then fading. Since she is at a distance, you do not want to fade her hair, etc.<br/> <br/>Outside of this, I think your image is very nice because the choice of the background is good and the pose is sweet and convincing. Further, even as is, the image conveys that unique fairy tale feel.</td>', 'from the critique Club: This was a very smart concept and even the choice for b/w was also wise. The only weakness is in the execution of the halo. Since the comp is okay and the photography is okay, let me concentrate on the effect.The way to do this is to select the figure after you have done all the levels adjustments, etc. After selection, copy the layer. Copy your background and draw an oval with 40 or 60 pixel feather. One way to finish is to fill the oval with white and then reduce the opacity to your liking. Then you paste the layer of the girl you originally copied. In essence, you have the actual background. On top you have a copy of the background and this layer is applied with just enough opacity to accentuate the halo. On top of this you paste the girl and the halo appears to come from the back while preserving the detail of the girl. This is superior to selecting her inversing and then fading. Since she is at a distance, you do not want to fade her hair, etc. Outside of this, I think your image is very nice because the choice of the background is good and the pose is sweet and convincing. Further, even as is, the image conveys that unique fairy tale feel.', '2004-09-11 22:26:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(905605, 100989, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dr rick:</b></div><hr/><i> Focus is nicely soft but the DOF is too narrow; an aperture one step smaller (f/4) would have put the whole subject in focus while still keeping the background unobtrusively blurry.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>True the focus is soft, maybe even just a little too soft around the eye area. If the eyes were a tad sharper this would be absolutely amazing, instead of just amazing :) I do have to disagree about the depth of field being too narrow though. I find the depth of field as it is very adequate. An f/4 aperture wouldn''t have done anything to benefit this image.</td>', 'Originally posted by dr rick: Focus is nicely soft but the DOF is too narrow; an aperture one step smaller (f/4) would have put the whole subject in focus while still keeping the background unobtrusively blurry.  True the focus is soft, maybe even just a little too soft around the eye area. If the eyes were a tad sharper this would be absolutely amazing, instead of just amazing :) I do have to disagree about the depth of field being too narrow though. I find the depth of field as it is very adequate. An f/4 aperture wouldn''t have done anything to benefit this image.', '2004-09-12 08:52:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(905721, 101033, 714, '<td valign="top">You did good here, Ami!  Congtrats on the top 20!<br/> <br/>I agree with VisiBlanco.  You should work on it and see what you come up with.<br/> <br/>Excellent photo!</td>', 'You did good here, Ami!  Congtrats on the top 20! I agree with VisiBlanco.  You should work on it and see what you come up with. Excellent photo!', '2004-09-12 11:36:19.000000', NULL, 0),
